WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.687
Team performance depends on shared mental models.

00:00:02.687 --> 00:00:07.121
People need a common understanding of goals, roles, constraints, current status, risks,

00:00:07.121 --> 00:00:08.230
and expected actions.

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:12.295
Without that shared picture, individuals may work hard in different directions.

00:00:12.295 --> 00:00:14.512
Communication is not just information exchange;

00:00:14.512 --> 00:00:18.207
it is how a team keeps its operating picture aligned.

00:00:18.207 --> 00:00:21.164
Clear handoffs and defined responsibilities reduce hidden work.

00:00:21.164 --> 00:00:25.968
A good handoff explains what changed, what remains unresolved, what decisions were made,

00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:29.663
what risks exist, and what the next person should do.

00:00:29.663 --> 00:00:34.098
Documentation supports continuity when people are absent, tired, new to the work,

00:00:34.098 --> 00:00:35.945
or operating across time zones.

00:00:35.945 --> 00:00:39.271
Work that exists only in someone's head is fragile.

00:00:39.271 --> 00:00:44.075
Psychological safety at a practical level means people can raise concerns, admit uncertainty,

00:00:44.075 --> 00:00:48.140
ask for help, and report mistakes without being punished for honesty.

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:50.357
It does not mean avoiding standards.

00:00:50.357 --> 00:00:54.422
It means the team can surface reality early enough to respond.

00:00:54.422 --> 00:00:59.965
High-performing teams make it safe to tell the truth and expected to improve the work.

00:00:59.965 --> 00:01:03.291
Meeting hygiene, escalation paths, and feedback culture all matter.

00:01:03.291 --> 00:01:05.878
Meetings should have purpose, ownership, and outcomes.

00:01:05.878 --> 00:01:08.834
Escalation paths should be clear before a crisis.

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:12.160
Feedback should be specific, timely, and tied to behavior.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:16.594
The goal is to make team performance less dependent on heroic individuals

00:01:16.594 --> 00:01:18.442
and more dependent on visible,

00:01:18.442 --> 00:01:19.181
repeatable coordination.

00:01:19.181 --> 00:01:21.398
Healthy teams also make work visible.

00:01:21.398 --> 00:01:25.094
Hidden assumptions, hidden blockers, and hidden overload create performance risk.

00:01:25.094 --> 00:01:29.159
Shared boards, written decisions, concise updates, and explicit ownership reduce ambiguity.

00:01:29.159 --> 00:01:31.746
When the team can see the work,

00:01:31.746 --> 00:01:36.180
it can rebalance priorities before individuals have to compensate through heroic effort.
